{"at_rifles(ger2)" "This team of anti-tank infantrymen is equipped with an anti-tank rifle, perfectly suited for taking out lightly armored enemy vehicles. While the high velocity rifle packs a punch, it is insufficient to take on heavier vehicles and it may require several shots to fully disable light vehicles."}
{"tankmans(ger2)" "This pair of tank crews are only lightly armed but are well-suited for crewing your armored vehicles and field guns. Use them to replace the losses you have suffered in combat and re-man your equipment. They are not suited for infantry combat and can't capture points."}
{"snipers_d(ger2)" "This well-trained marksman is armed with a scoped rifle and is capable of eliminating enemy infantry with precision, at long range. He relies on stealth to avoid detection while seeking to eliminate his targets. Use him to take out enemy officers or other important targets before engaging general infantry."}
{"snipers(ger2)" "This well-trained marksman is armed with a scoped rifle and is capable of eliminating enemy infantry with precision, at long range. He relies on stealth to avoid detection while seeking to eliminate his targets. Use him to take out enemy officers or other important targets before engaging general infantry."}
{"smgs2(ger2)" "A single infantryman armed with an MP-40 submachine gun and AT grenades."}
{"riflemans2(ger2)" "A single infantryman armed with a bolt-action K98 rifle and sandbags."}
{"flamers(ger2)" "This team of specialists comes equipped with a flamethrower which strikes terror into the hearts of the enemy. It is one of the deadliest weapons in close range combat, capable of igniting buildings and setting cover ablaze -- invaluable when seeking to ferret out the enemy. However, the fuel canister each troop carries  on his back is highly volatile and could lead to sudden and certain death if hit by enemy fire. Use these specialists wisely, as you only have few available for each battle."}
{"bazookers(ger2)" "This team of anti-tank rocket-launcher infantrymen is armed with a Panzerschreck and they are trained to destroy tanks in close combat using armor-piercing rockets. They are capable of destroying even the heaviest armored vehicles -- provided they can find a weakness to exploit. Beware of the armored skirts on some vehicles, as they greatly reduce the effectiveness of these shaped-charge rounds."}
{"stormtroopers(ger2)" "A squad of 12 elite jaegers, skill 8. The main purpose of the German Jaeger Divisions was to fight in adverse terrain where smaller, coordinated units were more facilely combat capable than the brute force offered by the standard infantry divisions. The Jaegers (means hunters in German) relied on a high degree of training, and slightly superior communications. They were among the prioritized to get new weapons such as the StG44 and G43. This elite jaeger squad includes an MG42 team, a sniper, and a rifle-grenadier, allowing for wide scale operation adaptability."}
{"elites_para(ger2)" "A squad of 12 apex paratroopers, skill 10. Battle-scarred Fallschirmjaegers who had undergone many battles and survived since the Battle of Crete, they were among the best men the Fatherland can offer. Includes a sniper, two MG42 teams, 2 FG42s, and 3 rifle-grenadiers."}
{"ap_miners(ger2)" "This team of specialists arrives with a full complement of anti-personnel mines which can be placed to provide the perfect defense against advancing infantry. Deploy them along likely routes of enemy advance or use them to secure a vulnerable flank from enemy attack."}
{"at_miners(ger2)" "This team of specialists arrives with a full complement of anti-tank mines which can be deployed to thwart advances made by enemy vehicles. Place them along roads or other likely routes of enemy advance. In some cases, a mine might only disable a vehicle, so be prepared to finish off any enemy vehicles which get disabled by your mines."}
{"officers(ger2)" "This experienced field officer is capable of supporting your troops by spotting enemy units from afar with his binoculars. Use his skill in locating enemy units through the fog of war, so that your other units can engage or avoid them as necessary. The officer also reduces your current CP by 17 which allows you to field a bigger army, and comes with two jaegers armed with StG44s as his personal bodyguards when surveying the front."}
